{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/98895-adventure-owod-crossover-kinda","id":98895,"title":"Adventure!/oWoD crossover? (kinda)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T20:08:59-07:00","id":98895,"title":"Adventure!/oWoD crossover? (kinda)","content":"Has anyone tried using elements from Adventure! to add an pulp action feel to their games? Like a mesmerist antagonist plotting against them. I can see it in a Society of Ether game, or something set in the 1930s/40s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T20:43:22-07:00","id":98912,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be more inclined to go with a Fusion setting instead of trying to cram the Inspired into the World of Darkness. Start with the World of Darkness\u2019 history right up through the early 20s, when Czar Vargo\u2019s attempt to derail the Technocracy\u2019s Timeline and to allow Ether Science to flourish was wildly successful \u2014 albeit at the cost of his life in a massive Paradox Backlash: the Avatar Storm appeared nearly a century early, and daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts started to appear alongside an upswing of linear mages. The Technocratic Union is thrown into disarray by the newly-manifest Avatar Storm; it will take them the better part of a century to reassert themselves. Meanwhile, the Ether Society supplants the Order of Hermes as the de facto leaders of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts are still among the ranks of the Conventions; they\u2019ll eventually abandon the Union in part due to the Union\u2019s bungled attempt to recruit and manipulate Doctor Primorius, but that\u2019s a generation away. Likewise, the Avatar Storm is going to subside; but that, too, will take decades.<br /> <br /> For this fusion, I would use MRev-style Resonance (now known as Synergy, IIRC). The reason is that the three types of Synergy align nicely with the three types of Inspiration: e.g., Static Synergy parallels the Reflective facet while Entropic Synergy parallels the Destructive facet and Dynamic Synergy parallels the Intuitive facet. <br /> <br /> Also for this fusion, I\u2019d go with the notion that daredevils are Paramorphs, and that sorcerers are \u201cproto-mages\u201d: or rather, <i>daredevils</i> are \u201cproto-mages\u201d whose Avatars are stirring and subconsciously warping reality in minor ways on the daredevil\u2019s behalf; and sorcerers are daredevils who still haven\u2019t Awakened, but have learned ways to consciously direct their slumbering Avatars through what\u2019s commonly referred to as magic. In short, Paths supplement Heroic Knacks. I\u2019m inclined to hack the Hedge Magic rules so that the Inspiration facets factor into them in various ways.<br /> <br /> oWoD-style Psychic Numina do not exist in this fusion; instead, they\u2019re replaced by the mesmerists\u2019 Psychic Knacks. Those that don\u2019t already have parallels among the Knacks can serve as inspiration for new Psychic Knacks. I\u2019m not yet sure how mesmerists and stalwarts differ from daredevils in terms of what they are, other than the fact that both involve fundamental transformations of the Avatar\u2019s nature.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I\u2019m thinking of this primarily as a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>/<b>Adventure!</b> fusion, as <b>Mage</b> (and particularly the Sons of Ether) is by far the most natural connection point. Frankly, I\u2019m not familiar enough with the other oWoD lines to comment on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-27-2014, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T12:17:53-07:00","id":99389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/98895-adventure-owod-crossover-kinda?p=98912#post98912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I\u2019m not familiar enough with the other oWoD lines to comment on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>W:tA: </b>At this point in time, both the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers were closely linked/associated with due to the Glass Walker camp, the Wise Guys.<br /> This is if you are going for Prohibition era type stories involving the Mafia/Gangs or if you want to do something inspired by Dick Tracy and Crime Story Pulps that were popular in the 30's/40's.<br /> <br /> You would also see a surge in the Glass Walker camp, Umbral Pilots, when space exploration became popular with the Pulps.<br /> <br /> Also, there was a Garou pack detailed out in W:tA (Silent Striders Revised) that was made for this sort of thing and inspired by it. (1920's to 30's Adventure Heroes):<br /> Vik Stryker (Silent Strider Gaillard)<br /> Lorna McNab (Fianna Philodox)<br /> Dr. Stratus (Glass Walker Theurge)<br /> Greta Cole (Shadow Lord Ragabash)<br /> An Lei Shing (Stargazer Ahroun)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 03-26-2014, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T12:39:17-07:00","id":99422,"title":"","content":"This Fusion sounds quite interesting and I shall want to explore it more. I was thinking more simply though: using Adventure! character creation to drop in interesting NPCs, not necessarily concerned with their origins (it's a weird world and weird people and things are bound to pop up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T14:06:05-07:00","id":99489,"title":"","content":"I planned this many years ago but had to drop it because POD &amp; Drive-through RPG didn't exist back then, so I couldn't get the PDF or physical copy from anywhere not even eBay","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T14:23:09-07:00","id":180080,"title":"","content":"I had a literal crossover game, once. An unfinished plotline from a Mage game I ran involving a Technocratic Construct that was slowly turning Nephandi. I was running an Aberrant game at the time, and the party came across an old device created by Nikola Tesla. No clue what it did... at first. Fight broke out over control of the device, it got activated/broken during the fight, and zapped the party into a different, parallel universe (ala Crosstime Travel). Put them in the OWoD universe; so, we had a bunch of novas running around, trying to figure out how the crap to get back home. They found some Etherites who could help, but all of their resources were being devoted to assaulting the Nephandi in the aforementioned Construct. The party joined in on the fight; at one point, we had Garou, Traditionalists, Kindred, Infernalists, HIT Marks, Widderslainte, Technocrats, Spirits embodied in force-grown flesh bodies, and Novas all fighting at once.<br /> <br /> It was beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}